@maxiloc @Jerskouille As we discussed maybe showing the current refinements (user selected refinements) even when there's no results, to allow the user to deselect some of them would be best?

If so we need another issue and an API proposal in every refinements (true by default) to do it.

Let me know if you want to deal with it.

It's fairly easy to implement, just tried it with refinement list, it's working well. 
One thing to note is that it needs autoHide to be true to have a good experience

For reference this is the code needed to do it

```
if (facetValues.length === 0) {
        facetValues = helper.getRefinements(facetName).map(function(facet) {
          return {
            count: 0,
            isRefined: true,
            name: facet.value,
            url: //fixme
          };
        });
      }
```
